From a6ee623ed5cd43b2e06f96fedccbd5a698609abc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: StonkGuy <68372320+StonkGuy@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 00:06:24 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] Syscalls: keep seccomp inheritance off the FEX_EXECVEFD path
 in execve

With a seccomp filter installed (FEX_NEEDSSECCOMP=1), every execve copies
the environment to add FEX_SECCOMPFD. That copy also entered the
FEX_EXECVEFD block whenever the target was not binfmt_misc compatible,
which is meant only for FD execs and for the path-backed loader FD:

- a path execve of a #! script (or of a foreign ELF) put
  FEX_EXECVEFD=-100 (AT_FDCWD) into the environment; the next FEX read
  the ELF from fd -100 and failed with "Invalid or Unsupported elf file",
  a foreign ELF passed the variable on to its own children
- an execveat(fd, "", AT_EMPTY_PATH) of a foreign ELF lost AT_EMPTY_PATH
  before the direct execveat and failed with ENOENT

Take the FEX_EXECVEFD path on the same condition as without seccomp.
Nothing changes when no filter is installed.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 Source/Tools/LinuxEmulation/LinuxSyscalls/Syscalls.cpp | 9 +++++++--
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/Source/Tools/LinuxEmulation/LinuxSyscalls/Syscalls.cpp b/Source/Tools/LinuxEmulation/LinuxSyscalls/Syscalls.cpp
index 207c33b..96d0c99 100644
--- a/Source/Tools/LinuxEmulation/LinuxSyscalls/Syscalls.cpp
+++ b/Source/Tools/LinuxEmulation/LinuxSyscalls/Syscalls.cpp
@@ -340,7 +340,12 @@ uint64_t ExecveHandler(FEXCore::Core::CpuStateFrame* Frame, const char* pathname
   // - seccomp inheritance
   // - FEXServer FD inheritance (unshare(CLONE_NEWNET))
   // - FD_CLOEXEC set on FD on anonymous file FD.
-  const bool NeedsEnvpCopy = (IsFDExec && !(IsBinfmtCompatible || IsOtherELF)) || HasSeccomp || NeedsFDCopy || NeedsLoaderFD;
+  // The FD to execute is handed to the next FEX through `FEX_EXECVEFD`: an FD execveat that binfmt_misc can't handle,
+  // or a path exec that has to keep its resolved host ELF open.
+  // Seccomp inheritance alone must not take this path: a path exec has no FD to hand over (Args.dirfd is AT_FDCWD), and
+  // an FD exec of a foreign ELF goes straight to the kernel, which still needs AT_EMPTY_PATH.
+  const bool NeedsExecveFD = (IsFDExec && !(IsBinfmtCompatible || IsOtherELF)) || NeedsFDCopy || NeedsLoaderFD;
+  const bool NeedsEnvpCopy = NeedsExecveFD || HasSeccomp;
 
   // We are trying to execute a shebang handled by a different architecture interpreter (e.g. /usr/bin/python from the host FS).
   // In this case we just defer to the kernel.
@@ -356,7 +361,7 @@ uint64_t ExecveHandler(FEXCore::Core::CpuStateFrame* Frame, const char* pathname
       }
     }
 
-    if (!IsBinfmtCompatible || NeedsFDCopy) {
+    if (NeedsExecveFD) {
       if (NeedsFDCopy) {
         // FEX needs the FD to live past execve when binfmt_misc isn't used,
         // so duplicate the FD if FD_CLOEXEC is set, which removes the FD_CLOEXEC flag.
